topics.detail:
Russia Aggression argues that Russia is acting aggressively. Trump Ukraine Deal argues that Trump's Ukraine deal is ridiculous. Trump's allies are benefiting from Ukraine talks. Trump's administration is corrupt in Ukraine dealings. Ukraine aid is being diverted for Trump's gain. Trump's Ukraine policy is morally indecent.

@twmcltd.bsky.social: “Ukraine alleges Russia laid a disgusting trap, using a young kid to detain a Ukrainian woman. Liubov Rozhanska was sent this video of her grandson "about to fly to Kazakhstan." The woman flew to meet him and bring him home, only for Kazakhstan to arrest her on Russia's behalf.”

Russia Aggression (61.2%) says Russia is acting aggressively. Trump Ukraine Deal (38.8%) says Trump's Ukraine talks involve an oil deal benefiting his allies.

Iran War argues that US lacks exit strategy in Iran war. War with Iran affects American power. War with Iran leads to wider conflict. Iran says no military solution to war. War with Iran argues that Trump plans to blame Iran for false flag attacks. Trump's invasion of Iran endangers allies. Trump's war with Iran is based on lies. Trump's actions towards Iran are reckless and threatening. Trump's decision to go to war with Iran caused an energy shock. Trump Invitation argues that Trump invites Iran to bomb Los Angeles or San Diego. Trump thinks Iran taking out LA or San Diego is a small price to pay. Trump suggests letting Iran attack US cities to keep the world safe.

@mgearsolidarity.bsky.social: “Tell me more about how we want to be on America's side "when it all kicks off" now the Iran War has made some things more obvious to the more traditionally minded among you.”

Iran War (48.9%) says US faces challenges in war with Iran. War with Iran (36%) says Trump is escalating conflict with Iran. Trump Invitation (15.1%) says Trump suggests Iran can attack US cities.

Diesel Prices argues that Diesel Don is tanking the GOP with high diesel prices. High diesel prices are hurting Americans. Diesel prices are unstable and need to be fixed. Oil Release argues that G7 is releasing oil reserves to ease pressure on energy markets. Releasing oil reserves does not solve the underlying supply problem. Oil companies benefit from high and volatile oil prices due to destabilized energy markets. Fuel Costs argues that most fossil fuel costs are externalities, not subsidies. high fuel prices are a global issue. governments subsidize fossil fuels, making them expensive compared to clean energy. High Gas Prices argues that High gas prices will lead to Trump's downfall. A product will not impact gas prices. Promises to cut gas prices are broken. War raises gas prices. Gas prices are unaffordable for families. Releasing more oil can bring prices down.

@jhoegg.bsky.social: “I’m simultaneously relieved that I got rid of my oil furnace this year and terrified for all the families who are facing these home heating oil prices. 😢 $400 ￼ it’s not gonna go far”

Diesel Prices (32.8%) says Diesel prices are too high. Oil Release (27.9%) says G7 releases oil reserves to ease pressure on global fuel supplies. Fuel Costs (21.3%) says Fuel costs are high. High Gas Prices (18%) says Gas prices are too high.

City Cheated argues that City cheated to break into the top four. City disrespected sporting integrity. City's spending inflated the market and hurt other clubs. Football Cheating argues that City fans overlook their club's cheating. Manchester City's cheating mocks other fans. The football world will loathe Manchester City. The BBC sympathizes with cheating wealthy clubs. Wealthy clubs' cheating is ignored in football discussions.

@gobb.ie: “The keep politics out of football brigade don't like it up 'em.”

City Cheated (77.1%) says City cheated to succeed. Football Cheating (22.9%) says Wealthy clubs cheat in football.

US Canada Tensions argues that Canada faces threats from the US. Quebec Independence argues that Foreign interference may influence Quebec's referendum. Quebec voters should make their voices heard. Indigenous people in Quebec should vote to demand action. The US may exploit Quebec's independence movement. A Quebec independence referendum would be problematic. Quebec's separatist party may lead to another referendum. Alberta Separation argues that Alberta is threatened from within and by the US. Alberta's separatists may team up with personal injury lawyers. Important assets should not be placed in Alberta due to separation risks.

@davidhamer1951.bsky.social: “One of the Alberta traitors. 🍁😠🍁”

US Canada Tensions (44%) says Canada faces threats from the US. Quebec Independence (36%) says Quebec may become independent. Alberta Separation (20%) says Alberta may separate from Canada.

Women Oppressed argues that Feminism is demonised and women are bullied. Women have been oppressed for centuries. Patriarchy rewards behaviour that harms women. Women's voices have been quieter. Men Attack Women argues that Women are attacked online for pointing out men's responsibility. Men attack women on social media for standing up for themselves. Men are quick to threaten women online. Men use violence against women when disagreed with.

@tpwrtrmnky.bsky.social: “"Feminism needs to expand to also deal with men's issues" ok but. quick question. are you absolutely certain that it's done the work to deal with the issues faced by all women? cause like. i think feminism. the one that's centered on women. should do that first.”

Women Oppressed (68.6%) says Women are oppressed. Men Attack Women (31.4%) says Men attack women online for speaking out.

Medicare For All argues that Medicare should be for all. Medicare Payment argues that Trump's $90 payment is insufficient for seniors' health expenses. The $90 payment is a bribe considering upcoming Medicare premium hikes. The payment is a small consolation after gutting social programs. The $90 payment is an insult given the high costs of Medicare and prescription drugs.

@thetnholler.bsky.social: “Medicare for All. Now. 🇺🇸 😕”

Medicare For All (59.6%) says Medicare should be for all. Medicare Payment (40.4%) says Trump offers $90 to Medicare seniors.
